# Compact Action Dialog Standard

All portal **dialogs** (create, edit, assign, confirm, print options, etc.)
must use the shared template in
`src/components/forms/compact-action-dialog.tsx`.

Do **not** build custom `DialogContent` / `DialogHeader` / `DialogFooter`
chrome. New dialogs and any dialog you touch must migrate to this template.

## Required structure

```tsx
import {
  CompactActionDialogBody,
  CompactActionDialogContent,
  CompactActionDialogFooter,
  CompactActionDialogHeader,
  compactActionDialogFormClassName, // taller form dialogs only
} from "@/components/forms/compact-action-dialog";
import { Dialog } from "@/components/ui/dialog";

<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}>
  <CompactActionDialogContent className="sm:max-w-lg">
    <CompactActionDialogHeader
      icon={SomeLucideIcon}
      title={t("…")}
      description={t("…")}
    />
    <CompactActionDialogBody>{/* fields / copy */}</CompactActionDialogBody>
    <CompactActionDialogFooter
      onCancel={() => onOpenChange(false)}
      submitLabel={t("common.actions.save")}
      submitType="submit" // or onSubmit + type button
      isSubmitting={busy}
      error={error}
    />
  </CompactActionDialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

Reference implementations: `assign-appointment-route-dialog.tsx`,
`employee-title-dialog.tsx`.

## Rules

1. **Always** wrap body chrome with `CompactActionDialogContent` (not raw
   `DialogContent`). It owns mobile bottom-sheet layout, `gap-0` / `p-0`, and
   `FormDialogChromeProvider`.
2. **Header** → `CompactActionDialogHeader` with a Lucide `icon` when the
   action has a clear metaphor (Route, Plus, Save, Printer, …).
3. **Body** → `CompactActionDialogBody` for scrollable content between header
   and footer. Do not put primary actions in the body.
4. **Footer** → `CompactActionDialogFooter`. Prefer built-in Cancel / primary
   props; pass `children` only for custom action sets. Use `error` / `warning`
   for footer notices.
5. **Taller forms** → add `compactActionDialogFormClassName` on
   `CompactActionDialogContent` (or the inner `form`) so sections scroll in the
   body while header/footer stay pinned.
6. **Copy** → localize every user-visible string (`en` + `es`). Prefer
   `common.actions.*` for Cancel / Save / shared labels.
7. **When editing a legacy dialog** that still uses raw `DialogContent`,
   migrate it to this template in the same change — do not extend the old
   chrome.

## Not this rule (keep existing patterns)

- **Sheets / record view** — `Sheet` / `RecordViewSheet`, not dialogs
- **Non-modal surfaces** — popovers, dropdowns, command palettes
- **`ui/dialog.tsx` primitives** — still used underneath; feature code imports
  `Dialog` + CompactAction* helpers, not bespoke content chrome

## Checklist

- [ ] Uses `CompactActionDialogContent` / `Header` / `Body` / `Footer`
- [ ] No custom padded `DialogContent` header/footer layout
- [ ] Icon + localized title/description on the header
- [ ] Actions live in `CompactActionDialogFooter`
- [ ] Touched legacy dialogs migrated, not copied
